  "scope": "Published Hornkohl/Parigger Swan data with one declared absolute anchor.\n\nResearch only. The 2015 archive contains 29,004 lines identical to the 2023\nthree-column reformat. Its dimensional strength unit is not established.\nPreserve every relative strength and set ONE common coefficient from Brooke\n2013 Table 7 A(0,0)=7.626e6 /s. Use the unambiguous J'=0, v'=v''=0 pair;\nBrooke's band rate is from J'=1, Omega'=0, so this is a rotationless-band\ncalibration approximation, not a recovered original unit conversion.\nOther low-v band rates and laboratory lifetimes are independent checks.\n\nNo stellar parameter, width, band multiplier or opacity area is fitted.\nAll source records are retained, including coincident records. No ExoMol\nSwan lines are silently added to the Hornkohl-only calculation.\n",
